x I think the "resolver" question is pretty easy. We already have a common concept that every
x airway/procedure ends up turning into a concrete list of waypoints in the flight plan (both for
x the UI inside the procedure container, and because that's what gets concetated to make the
x physical waypoint list to draw on the screen). So "resolving" an entry is just taking the first
x item in the list, and resolving the exit is just the last. I think you may have overthought
x "resolving" in the airway case, and specialized it to airways.
x 
x "clean geometric “exit point” for downstream bridging. ... vectors" Yeah, I think this
x represents a "gap" in the flight plan. I think we might represent this as a concrete waypoint
x called "vectors"; that's the last waypoint in the concretized procedure. When the UI sees that,
x it knows there's a discontinuity here that affects drawing and sequencing.
x "  - A procedure may need a notion of unresolved or suspended continuation." Yep!
x 
x "Not every enroute transition works with every runway transition." -- so that affects
