Let's draw airspace boundaries.

  On FAA boundary sources: I found official FAA indications that boundary-ish data is available as services, but not yet a clean
  static polygon product I’d build against.

  - FAA’s aeronautical data/products page explicitly lists Special Use Airspace and Temporary Flight Restrictions (TFR) under Servi
    ces: https://www.faa.gov/data/aero_data (https://www.faa.gov/data/aero_data)
  - FAA’s aeronautical data page points to the AIS data ecosystem generally:
    https://www.faa.gov/air_traffic/flight_info/aeronav/aero_data (https://www.faa.gov/air_traffic/flight_info/aeronav/aero_data)
  - The AIM/AIP material confirms SUA is authoritative FAA airspace content, but that’s descriptive text, not a geometry download:
      - https://www.faa.gov/air_traffic/publications/atpubs/aip_html/part2_enr_section_5.1.html
        (https://www.faa.gov/air_traffic/publications/atpubs/aip_html/part2_enr_section_5.1.html)
      - https://www.faa.gov/air_traffic/publications/atpubs/aim_html/chap3_section_4.html
        (https://www.faa.gov/air_traffic/publications/atpubs/aim_html/chap3_section_4.html)



